  {
   "name": "Grit Bloom",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "per-voice drive",
    "per-voice pan",
    "evolving"
   ],
   "description": "A clean pad that grows grit: a slow mod envelope raises each note's distortion drive and cutoff, and moves the note out from the centre, each one to its own random side. As it blooms the filter's resonance rises and a slow per-note LFO starts sweeping that peak through the upper harmonics, every note at its own phase, so the top end shimmers and shifts while the grit grows. Macros: grit, bloom, shimmer.",
