  {
   "name": "Sub Fold",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "wavefolder",
    "per-voice drive",
    "sub"
   ],
   "description": "A pure sine sub, with a quiet sine an octave up so it carries on small speakers. A short mod envelope and velocity drive each note's attack into a wavefolder (sine distortion) in front of a keytracked ladder whose envelope lets the folds through only at the start, so the note settles back to a round sub. Macros: fold, octave.",
