  {
   "name": "Just Bells",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bells",
   "tags": [
    "microtuning",
    "just intonation",
    "FM"
   ],
   "description": "Two-operator FM bells (phase modulation, the way the DX7 does FM): a sine modulator at 3.5 times the pitch, its index struck high and falling away, so each bell starts clangorous and rings out towards a pure tone. Two unison copies a few cents apart beat like a real bell. Tuned to 5-limit just intonation on C (a Scala scale saved with the program), so thirds and fifths are beat-free in the key of C. Macros: strike, ring.",
