  {
   "name": "Doppler Flyby",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "fx",
   "tags": [
    "per-voice pan",
    "one-shot LFO",
    "doppler"
   ],
   "description": "Each note flies past: a one-shot ramp sweeps it across the stereo field, in a random direction for every note, while a second one-shot LFO with a drawn S-curve holds the pitch high on the approach and drops it sharply as the note passes, about a fifth down, brightest at the closest point. Hold notes for the full pass. Macros: distance, drop.",
